Caleb, Lucille,<br />
<br />
Memo of my call with Rosalind Tenniel this morning is attached for the file=
. In substance: Torvane has decided, at the CEO's direction and with the op=
erations committee's concurrence, not to assert the warranty claim against =
Brandt Thermal Systems, in view of the sole-source supply relationship. Tor=
vane does not want a tolling agreement sought, and does not want the claim =
raised with Brandt in any form.<br />
<br />
I walked Rosalind through the consequences in plain terms - including that =
the claim will in all likelihood be time-barred by late 2014 and that this =
is a business decision Torvane is entitled to make but cannot easily unmake=
 later. She understood, and she is comfortable. I asked her to confirm the =
decision and the resulting scope of our engagement in writing, and she will=
 send that confirmation tomorrow.<br />
<br />
Caleb - hold any further Brandt work. Lucille - leave the limitations tickl=
er in place until the written confirmation arrives, then see my note tomorr=
ow.<br />
<br />
Arthur
